            {
                "entry_id": "551fe61f-e318-3406-9ffd-de328d77332c",
                "word": "complotisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9c5d0070-c009-4526-a4aa-b878a4c41a7d",
                        "entry_id": "551fe61f-e318-3406-9ffd-de328d77332c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "complotismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "958bef42-ce78-3fa4-bf9b-4821f9bf0714",
                        "entry_id": "551fe61f-e318-3406-9ffd-de328d77332c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Conviction qu’une théorie du complot est à l’œuvre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "474b2904-1ca1-45a3-985a-70a7681a5bd6",
                                "sense_id": "958bef42-ce78-3fa4-bf9b-4821f9bf0714",
                                "text": "Désir sous-tendu par une sourde méfiance à l’égard du discours « des institutions », qui montre que les médias « mainstream », sur certains sujets, peuvent aussi flirter avec le complotisme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18f0875b-7663-4266-95f2-99d2ac462820",
                                "sense_id": "958bef42-ce78-3fa4-bf9b-4821f9bf0714",
                                "text": "Depuis une semaine, le nom de McKinsey s’est pourtant immiscé dans la campagne présidentielle : tous les adversaires d’Emmanuel Macron s’en sont emparés pour dénoncer « un scandale », quand ses soutiens, eux, ont crié au « complotisme » sans convaincre personne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d78d2d9-28ab-4604-8f3e-e5b90693b3ca",
                                "sense_id": "958bef42-ce78-3fa4-bf9b-4821f9bf0714",
                                "text": "« Voilà où mène le complotisme, la délégitimation d’un président démocratiquement élu », a dénoncé l’eurodéputé macroniste Stéphane Séjourné."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9c4c4a9-80ec-4cb8-86d3-bdf74eff0ea1",
                        "source_entry_id": "551fe61f-e318-3406-9ffd-de328d77332c",
                        "source_sense_id": "958bef42-ce78-3fa4-bf9b-4821f9bf0714",
                        "target_lang_word": "Verschwörung",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Verschwörung",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee0e7b78-451d-36cb-b98d-630bbb454f24",
                                        "entry_id": "47963e7b-687d-388a-a546-56a9ffee7736",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "gemeinsame und verdeckte Planung von Handlungen zum Nachteil Anderer"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17de0f4b-d8b6-4f0d-a429-eef246a3412e",
                                                "sense_id": "ee0e7b78-451d-36cb-b98d-630bbb454f24",
                                                "text": "„Doch zugleich sind die USA auch das Land realer und imaginierter Verschwörungen und ein Eldorado der Verschwörungstheoretiker. “"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "002f7ab7-868d-4e7f-ba00-56e02620e3cb",
                        "source_entry_id": "551fe61f-e318-3406-9ffd-de328d77332c",
                        "source_sense_id": "958bef42-ce78-3fa4-bf9b-4821f9bf0714",
                        "target_lang_word": "conspiracy theory",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "conspiracy theory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad3be908-e4eb-322c-8c66-e12e94467b17",
                                        "entry_id": "c2b7784a-084f-3526-9ff1-4c8b101851cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see conspiracy, theory. A hypothesis that posits conspiracy or collusion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd9ab6fe-a469-4d40-afc8-2193cddbd369",
                                                "sense_id": "ad3be908-e4eb-322c-8c66-e12e94467b17",
                                                "text": "England has had quite enough to do in Europe and Asia, without going out of her way to meddle with America. It was a physical and moral impossibility that she could be carrying on a gigantic conspiracy against us. But our masses, having only a rough general knowledge of foreign affairs, and not unnaturally somewhat exaggerating the space which we occupy in the world's eye, do not appreciate the complications which rendered such a conspiracy impossible. They only look at the sudden right-about-face movement of the English Press and public, which is most readily accounted for on the conspiracy theory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf8f319f-3d05-446a-a7eb-7b7dd05acdbe",
                                                "sense_id": "ad3be908-e4eb-322c-8c66-e12e94467b17",
                                                "text": "(A) conspiracy theory is simply a theory that posits a conspiracy – a secret plan on the part of some group to influence events by partly secret means."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62b823fe-50a6-4070-89ee-1a0a0e9b7eca",
                                                "sense_id": "ad3be908-e4eb-322c-8c66-e12e94467b17",
                                                "text": "The main problem with any particular conspiracy theory is not that it's wrong, but that it's inarguable; not that it's false, but that it is unfalsifiable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "267aa665-0e32-4f06-86f3-99b186015bbd",
                                                "sense_id": "ad3be908-e4eb-322c-8c66-e12e94467b17",
                                                "text": "It is impossible, within the limits set for this Answer, to deal in any detail with the conspiracy theory which Dr. Boyd has put forward with such virulence for so many years and which apparently has been adopted by His Majesty's Government, at least in part."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ef6e635-409c-4aaf-bb81-9691992c3bb4",
                                                "sense_id": "ad3be908-e4eb-322c-8c66-e12e94467b17",
                                                "text": "Signalgate must have been deliberate; tariffs must be a grand plan to crash the dollar in the interest of one economic faction or another. The risk is that ever-more elaborate explanations for stupid actions end up wrongly according those actions a kind of intelligence – rather confirming the insight of the political scientist Robyn Marasco that “conspiracy theory is a love affair with power that poses as its critique”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a82c513-39fb-3c11-bad2-d3ce937bc313",
                                        "entry_id": "c2b7784a-084f-3526-9ff1-4c8b101851cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hypothetical speculation that is commonly considered untrue or outlandish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e857402-ad6f-4a2b-869c-f050ccae9873",
                                                "sense_id": "1a82c513-39fb-3c11-bad2-d3ce937bc313",
                                                "text": "Before discussing Norman Mailer's magisterial bid for dominance in this field, I want to use Richard Cordon to anticipate a common liberal objection - the objection that all this is 'conspiracy theory'. One has become used to this stolid, complacent return serve: so apparently grounded in reason and scepticism but so often naive and one-dimensional."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af4a0546-66db-4411-b132-107a33614ee4",
                                                "sense_id": "1a82c513-39fb-3c11-bad2-d3ce937bc313",
                                                "text": "“So, like I’m Rock Hudson? I’m not sure that’s the answer.”\n “Ah,” Lola smiles knowingly, “that’s all just a conspiracy theory. He enjoyed the ladies too.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "472855f4-25fb-492f-a7f2-97c0220cc44f",
                                                "sense_id": "1a82c513-39fb-3c11-bad2-d3ce937bc313",
                                                "text": "QAnon, whose supporters also call it “The Storm\" or “Great Awakening,” is a wide-ranging conspiracy theory that burst into greater visibility this summer, after supporters at a Trump rally wearing Q shirts prompted a rush of national media coverage about it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "015782bd-56ca-444c-a8aa-feba8a20a8bd",
                                                "sense_id": "1a82c513-39fb-3c11-bad2-d3ce937bc313",
                                                "text": "Conspiracy theories can be comforting, a way to get one’s bearings during rapid change in the culture or the economy, by providing narratives that bring order."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef5dfc75-e36f-4f65-a7b4-0c8fe236d11a",
                                                "sense_id": "1a82c513-39fb-3c11-bad2-d3ce937bc313",
                                                "text": "President Donald Trump’s presidential memorandum ordering an investigation of Joe Biden’s cognitive decline and his use of the autopen […] is also nonsensical fan service, amplifying addled MAGA conspiracy theories that contend, with a straight face, that Biden was really a robotic clone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5687bef2-1a90-4963-8a44-5d53dbe7d439",
                                                "sense_id": "1a82c513-39fb-3c11-bad2-d3ce937bc313",
                                                "text": "\"MAGA really wouldn't exist without conspiracy theories,\" said Eric Alterman, a journalism professor at Brooklyn College. \"These theories don't require evidence. They're about stories people tell themselves to explain why things feel like they're going wrong in their lives.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
